+# Result — ptc-revalidate (PeTTaChainer chaining verdict at pinned shas)
+
+**Verdict: backward chaining is BROKEN at the pins; forward chaining WORKS, with a
+caveat.** The April 2026 blocker is not fixed. Filed upstream as
+<https://github.com/rTreutlein/PeTTaChainer/issues/1>. Ledger row **S1 is reproduced,
+not cleared** — see "Ledger" below.
+
+Pins: PeTTaChainer `02a85c63be6a735f50f50e1084a717b3256b8406` (2026-07-20) ·
+PeTTa `43705f5d9ff8958ffe7f0aa6777fb8477f2401f2` (2026-07-24, = `pins.env` `PETTA_SHA`) ·
+SWI-Prolog 9.3.33 · Python 3.10.18 (uv-managed) · janus-swi 1.5.2.
+
+## What shipped
+
+In the code repo (`plnbench`), on branch `ptc-revalidate` (unmerged — merging is the
+operator's act):
+
+| path | what |
+|---|---|
+| `docs/ptc-verdict.md` | **the deliverable** — status per chaining mode at named shas, both test suites verbatim, the April probe re-run, what was ruled out, consequences for the roadmap |
+| `tests/ptc-revalidate/run.sh` | one-command re-derivation from a clean clone: clones both subjects at the pins, builds PeTTaChainer's own isolated task environment, runs four legs, re-reads the verdict off the output. Exit 0 = verdict holds, 2 = upstream moved, 1 = could not run |
+| `tests/ptc-revalidate/probes/*` | the minimal repro, the April format-A ProofWriter probe (+ a CTV control), and the same probe through the python API under both rule taggings |
+| `tests/ptc-revalidate/captured/` | the exact logs behind every number in the verdict, including two control runs |
+| `tests/ptc-revalidate/upstream-issue.md` | the upstream filing as sent |
+| `docs/known-issues.md` | new entry #6 (this finding, with disposition); #2's disposition updated — it rode along in the same issue, as the order asked |
+
+Three findings, not one:
+
+1. **Backward `query` returns empty for every goal** — including a goal that is a fact
+   `compileadd` just stored, and including facts `forward-chain` derived. 44 of 50 of
+   PeTTaChainer's own MeTTa tests and 7 of 16 of its python tests fail on exactly this.
+   `test_forward_backward_compose.metta` — the file April named — fails in April's shape:
+   `is (), should (: (r2 (r1 a0)) (Goal) (STV 1.0 0.999700089898053)). ❌`
+2. **Forward chaining works** — on the April ProofWriter theory it derives
+   `(Like cow_1 squirrel_1)` at `(STV 1.0 0.8181611546663258)` with the right proof term,
+   and saturation correctly stops there, leaving the two gold-Unknown questions
+   underivable. So this theory's four findings-table answers are all recoverable today by
+   forward chaining plus a KB read.
+3. **…but only for rules tagged `(CTV …)`.** A rule tagged `(STV s c)` — which is what
+   translation format A emits, and what upstream's `pln_validator` and
+   `test_stv_implication_derived_ctv.metta` both say is supported — compiles (it adds the
+   same rule rows) and then never fires. Nothing derived, no error.
+
+All three fail silently: empty result, exit status 0, no diagnostic. That is the ledger
+S3 class, and it is why the verdict insists a harness must attribute empty output rather
+than map it to Unknown.
+
+## How verified
+
+- **Both upstream suites, in upstream's own declared environment.** PeTTaChainer ships
+  `.myclaw/Dockerfile` + `.myclaw/environment.json`; the harness builds that image and
+  runs that `test` command. Python: `Ran 16 tests … FAILED (failures=5, errors=2)`.
+  MeTTa: `Summary: 6 passed, 44 failed`. Logs committed.
+- **Ground-truth discipline.** Every probe prints; nothing asserts. The verdict quotes
+  captured output, and `run.sh` re-derives each mode's status from that output rather
+  than from a human's memory of it. No expected value in this task was written before the
+  runtime produced it.
+- **Controls, because "your environment is broken" is the obvious rebuttal.**
+  PeTTa@43705f5's own example suite is green in the same image (157 `OK:`, 0 failures,
+  exit 0). Re-running the whole MeTTa suite against PeTTa@d9a437c — `main` as of
+  2026-07-20, contemporary with the chainer sha and *before* PR #212's quoting change —
+  gives identical per-file verdicts on every chainer test (5/45; the one delta is a
+  lib_pln example unrelated to chaining). PeTTa@4a62d08 (the pre-#212 merge parent)
+  reproduces the empty query too. The minimal repro is also empty at eleven older
+  PeTTaChainer commits back to 2026-06-12.
+- **Two full end-to-end runs** of `tests/ptc-revalidate/run.sh` from re-cloned checkouts,
+  the second after the review fixes; identical per-file verdicts both times.
+- **Review: `/code-review` at medium, run against the code clone**, on the two-commit
+  branch. Five findings, all in the harness's failure handling, all fixed in
+  `6087f43`: legs 3 and 4 now fail loudly instead of letting a missing measurement read
+  as "upstream moved"; an unrecognised probe result reads `UNPARSED` and stops rather
+  than defaulting to WORKS; the container writes its venv and `.pyc` outside the bind
+  mount so a rootful engine leaves nothing undeletable; the python-API probe now runs
+  both rule taggings, so the forward-only design the verdict recommends is evidenced on
+  the surface the pipeline arm would use. The review independently re-checked every
+  quantitative claim in the verdict against the logs and the checkouts.
+- **Not verified:** why the backward chainer returns nothing. Diagnosing it means reading
+  the backward chainer's internals, and PeTTaChainer is a subject under test — the
+  charter says findings get filed, not fixed. The issue says plainly that we are not
+  claiming a cause.
+
+## To operate
+
+**Rerun the verdict** (about six minutes on a warm host; needs git, podman or docker, and
+network for the two clones):
+
+```bash
+cd <plnbench>
+bash tests/ptc-revalidate/run.sh
+# exit 0 = the recorded verdict still holds
+# exit 2 = a mode's status CHANGED — upstream moved; read results/ptc-revalidate/*.log,
+#          then update docs/ptc-verdict.md (and this ledger row)
+# exit 1 = a leg could not run (environment)
+```
+
+Offline, or to pin elsewhere:
+
+```bash
+PTC_SRC=/path/PeTTaChainer.bundle PETTA_SRC=/path/PeTTa.bundle bash tests/ptc-revalidate/run.sh
+ENGINE=docker PTC_SHA=<sha> PETTA_SHA=<sha> bash tests/ptc-revalidate/run.sh
+```
+
+Everything lands in `results/ptc-revalidate/` (gitignored): four logs, the image build
+log, and the scratch checkouts under `work/`. `KEEP_WORKDIR=1` reuses them. The named
+volumes `plnbench-ptc-uv-cache` and `plnbench-ptc-uv-python` keep uv's cache and its
+managed CPython 3.10 warm; they are safe to delete, the next run refills them. Image tag:
+`plnbench-ptc:02a85c6` — distinct from anything the stack runs.
+
+**The two controls**, if a maintainer asks (both from `results/ptc-revalidate/work/`,
+after a normal run):
+
+```bash
+# PeTTa's own suite in the same image
+podman run --rm -v $PWD:/work:z -v $PWD/PeTTa:/nexus/Dev/OpenCog/PeTTa:z \
+  -w /nexus/Dev/OpenCog/PeTTa -e LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 plnbench-ptc:02a85c6 sh test.sh
+
+# the MeTTa suite against a different PeTTa (worktree it first)
+git -C PeTTa worktree add --detach ../petta-alt/d9a437c d9a437c
+podman run --rm -v $PWD:/work:z -v $PWD/petta-alt/d9a437c:/nexus/Dev/OpenCog/PeTTa:z \
+  -w /work/src/PeTTaChainer/pettachainer/metta -e LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 plnbench-ptc:02a85c6 ./test.sh
+```
+
+**What the pipeline arm needs to know** (`folio-parser-arm`, and any ProofWriter run that
+was going to use PeTTaChainer):
+
+- Do not design around `query`. It returns empty for everything at these pins, including
+  direct fact lookup. Any arm that queries is blocked until upstream moves — watch the
+  issue, or run `run.sh` and watch for exit 2.
+- A forward-only design is viable **today**: `compileadd` the theory, `forward-chain` to
+  saturation, read `&kb` (or `forward-has-derived?`). On the April ProofWriter theory that
+  yields the correct answers.
+- If you do that, **emit rules with CTV truth values** — `(CTV (STV s c) (STV 0.0 1.0))`,
+  not `(STV s c)`. Format A as the semantic-parser emits it produces rules that compile
+  and never fire; nothing warns you. If a translation layer stays on format A, it needs a
+  rule-TV rewrite step, and that step needs its own test.
+- Treat empty output as a failure to attribute, never as Unknown — with these defects, an
+  unattributed harness would score every question "Unknown" and look like it ran fine.
+- Do not vendor PeTTaChainer into `pins.env` yet. The seeding comment's reasoning still
+  holds, and this verdict is the evidence.
+
