+## Reflection
+
+**Against the order's predictions.** Effort landed inside the predicted 2–3 hours, but
+the risk mass was not where the order put it: the environment build was easy (upstream's
+own `.myclaw` image is genuinely turnkey — build, `uv sync --frozen`, run), and the cost
+went into *disconfirming* the finding. A verdict that says "your suite fails 44 of 50
+tests" is only worth filing if you have already killed the environment hypothesis, so
+most of the session went to controls: PeTTa's own suite, a contemporary PeTTa, a
+pre-PR-212 PeTTa, eleven older chainer commits. Questions asked: **0** — the order's named
+seam (SWI-Prolog/janus versions on the host) never opened, because the subject ships its
+own pinned toolchain. Review outcome: as predicted, no correctness defects in the finding;
+the five findings were all about how the *harness* fails, which is exactly what a
+verification task's review should catch.
+
+**The tension worth recording.** The order asks for a verdict per chaining mode, and the
+honest answer needed a third axis the order did not anticipate: rule truth-value tagging.
+"Forward chaining works" is true and would have been misleading on its own — the pipeline
+arm's own translation format is the one tagging that does not work. Splitting the verdict
+into three findings rather than two is the only decision I made beyond the order's letter,
+and it is the finding the pipeline arm will actually trip over.
+
+**For the improver.** This task is a clean instance of the findings loop closing at speed:
+the April control arm reported this blocker informally in April and it sat unrevalidated
+for four months; the hive instance took hours and produced something upstream can run.
+That is the S1 comparison, and it is the model-plus-process confound in miniature — the
+work was not hard, it was just *done*.
+
+**Surprise worth flagging to the next worker.** `PeTTaChainer.query(timeout_sec=0)` means
+"no timeout", not "expire immediately" (`pettachainer.py`), and the default (`10`) forks a
+`spawn` worker that re-adds every atom in a fresh process. Any harness calling this API
+should pass `timeout_sec=0` and impose its own wall clock, or it will pay a full KB replay
+per query — and, if run from a REPL, silently lose the timeout anyway.
